---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "About · Arhan Sibal";
const description =
  "Arhan Sibal grew up in Delhi, spent his career in Gurgaon, and now lives in San Francisco. A computer science background that turned into strategy and operations work.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="about">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <p>
      I grew up in Delhi and did not really leave until I was thirty. School
      there, computer science at IIIT Delhi there, and then my whole early
      career a short drive away in Gurgaon. The first time I lived anywhere
      else was Ann Arbor, for the MBA at Michigan Ross in 2023. I live in San
      Francisco now, and I am enjoying it more than I expected to.
    </p>

    <p>
      For the first stretch of my career I was the data and tools person. I
      wrote the SQL, built the models, and put together the things that made
      the analysis run. I was good at it and I liked it, but I was always one
      step removed from where the decisions got made.
    </p>

    <p>
      That changed in 2021. I got pulled onto client sites as the technical
      and strategy thought partner for front-end case teams, sitting in the
      room rather than supporting it from outside. My first on-site project
      was at a pharmaceutical manufacturing plant on the east coast of India.
      The problems shifted almost every day, the people around me were some of
      the sharpest I had worked with, and the work asked you to stay
      resourceful when the ground kept moving. I found I wanted to be in that
      room for good, not next to it. That is the year I decided to do an MBA,
      and I gave it one more year of that kind of work before applying.
    </p>

    <p>
      Since then I have worked across strategy, operations, and product, and
      the technical side has stayed with me the whole way. I still write my
      own SQL and Python, and when an off the shelf tool does not do what I
      need, I build one. The most recent of those is
      <a
        href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/cgbimjanhgfjcopnpklcikkpcbgmjgoo"
        >J.A.N.E.</a
      >, a Chrome extension for job seekers, built under MuggleTech, which is
      named after exactly the Harry Potter thing you are thinking of.
    </p>

    <p>
      Outside work, a fair amount of my time goes to my kitchen garden and to
      getting butter chicken right, which is harder than it sounds. On
      weekends I hike the Bluffs to Batteries trail, which is still the best
      argument I know for living in San Francisco. I am also slowly teaching
      myself guitar, and rewatching Harry Potter more often than a grown adult
      probably should.
    </p>

    <p class="about-close">
      If you want the formal version, it is on my
      <a href="/resume">resume</a>, or you can reach me at
      <a href="mailto:arhansibal10@gmail.com">arhansibal10@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .about h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 4.5vw, 2.2rem);
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .about p {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
  }

  .about-close {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
</style>
